      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Apply consented grouped Claw updates",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Extends `claws update <claw-or-agent> --from <source> --yes` behind `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1` to apply every grouped owner in `openclaw.clawUpdateResult.v1`.\n- Rebuilds and compares the read-only plan immediately before mutation, then advances root package/version/integrity provenance only after all owner executors succeed.\n- Applies managed workspace file add/change/remove through fs-safe rooted I/O with source digest checks, destination compare-and-swap checks, ownership updates, and guarded rollback.\n- Applies MCP add/change/remove through the validated config writer with create-only or expected-value CAS, including remote `sse` / `streamable-http` declarations and credential-free `auth: \"oauth\"`.\n- Applies cron add/change/remove through gateway-owned APIs. Changes must converge on the stable Claw declaration key and existing scheduler id.\n- Applies exact ClawHub skill/plugin package versions and updates package references. Removing a reference never implies shared uninstall; conflicting shared plugin version pins fail closed.\n- Rolls completed owners back in reverse order when a later owner or root provenance fails. Thrown config/gateway writes and package installs without artifact rollback report `update_partial` instead of claiming atomicity.\n- Keeps `--dry-run` read-only and requires explicit `--yes` consent.\n\nStack references:\n- RFC: openclaw/rfcs#27\n- Base PR: openclaw/openclaw#102959\n- Control UI plugin management alignment: openclaw/openclaw#103176\n\n## Ownership and Control UI alignment\n\nPackage references remain per-Claw provenance over shared skill/plugin artifacts. Update-time package removal releases only this Claw's reference. A plugin pinned to a different version by another Claw is not replaced. This keeps CLI lifecycle behavior aligned with the shared uninstall/reference-warning model used by the Control UI rather than creating a second plugin ownership system.\n\nPortable MCP declarations continue to use the validated config surface. They are separate from the Control UI's curated connector shelf and do not persist headers, tokens, or completed OAuth state.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nEnvironment: WSL2 Ubuntu 24.04 with isolated config and state.\n\nAn installed `@acme/update-proof@1.1.0` agent was previewed and updated to `1.2.0`:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw claws update update-proof --from ./target-grouped --dry-run --json\nopenclaw claws update update-proof --from ./target-grouped --yes --json\nopenclaw claws status update-proof --json\n```\n\nThe target changed the agent, added `SOUL.md` and `NOTES.md`, and added a remote `streamable-http` OAuth MCP server.\n\nObserved:\n- preview reported four unblocked grouped actions;\n- apply returned `openclaw.clawUpdateResult.v1` with `status: \"complete\"`;\n- both workspace files matched their target digests;\n- the MCP ownership record was `complete` and live state was `present`;\n- status reported version `1.2.0`, zero partial records, zero drift, and zero unresolved MCP references;\n- the original `addedAtMs` was preserved while `updatedAtMs` advanced.\n\nCron convergence and exact package installer behavior are covered with injected gateway/installer tests to avoid mutating a developer gateway or shared plugin installation during local proof.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 133 Claw, CLI, lifecycle, config, executor, rollback, and end-to-end tests across 19 files\n- non-incremental core TypeScript check: `tsgo -p tsconfig.json --noEmit --incremental false`\n- real isolated grouped preview -> consented apply -> status round trip\n- `git diff --check`\n",
        "branch": "user/giodl/claws-pr12-update-apply",
